# Implementation & Validation Checklist

Based on: /home/dr4zz/projects/nexus/speckit.specify

## Requirements Validation

- [ ] SSH sessions with detach/reattach (managed sessions with ring buffer)
- [ ] Standard SSH and Telnet sessions (native terminal)
- [ ] RDP and VNC via Ebiten GUI with IPC bridge
- [ ] YAML config with connections, groups, tags
- [ ] AES-256-GCM credential encryption with master password
- [ ] Health checking (TCP connect with latency)
- [ ] Connection list with table view, fuzzy filter, command mode
- [ ] Detail view, add/edit form, sessions view, event log
- [ ] Keyhint bar, help overlay, confirm dialogs
- [ ] SSH config import (~/.ssh/config parser)
- [ ] Clipboard copy (yank SSH command)
- [ ] F1.1 — Modal System (Normal/Insert/Visual/Command modes)**
- [ ] Normal mode is default. Every key is a command. No text input in Normal.
- [ ] Insert mode entered via `i`/`a`/`o` in text fields (filter, command, form fields).
- [ ] Command mode via `:` (ex commands) and `/` (search) and `?` (reverse search).
- [ ] Mode indicator in statusline: NORMAL (blue), INSERT (green), VISUAL (purple), COMMAND (yellow).
- [ ] `Esc` always returns to Normal mode. Universal cancel.
- [ ] Mode transitions fire events for statusline color change and cursor shape change.
- [ ] F1.2 — Neovim Motion Keys**
- [ ] `j`/`k` up/down in all lists and views.
- [ ] `h`/`l` for left/right panel navigation (when panels exist), column selection in tables.
- [ ] `gg` jump to first item. `G` jump to last item. `{count}G` jump to item N.
- [ ] `Ctrl+d`/`Ctrl+u` half-page scroll. `Ctrl+f`/`Ctrl+b` full-page scroll.
- [ ] `H`/`M`/`L` top/middle/bottom of visible screen.
- [ ] `{`/`}` jump between groups/sections in grouped lists.
- [ ] `w`/`b` next/previous group (word motion equivalent for lists).
- [ ] `0`/`$` first/last column in table views.
- [ ] `n`/`N` next/previous search match.
- [ ] `*` search for connection name under cursor. `#` reverse search.
- [ ] `f{char}` jump to next item starting with char. `;`/`,` repeat.
- [ ] Count prefix: `5j` moves down 5 items. `3dd` deletes 3 items.
- [ ] F1.3 — Operator + Motion Composition**
- [ ] `dd` delete current connection (with confirmation).
- [ ] `yy` yank/copy current connection details to clipboard.
- [ ] `p`/`P` paste connection (duplicate after/before current).
- [ ] `dG` delete from current to end (with confirmation for bulk).
- [ ] `dgg` delete from current to start (with confirmation for bulk).
- [ ] Operators work with Visual mode selections.
- [ ] F1.4 — Leader Key + Which-Key Popup**
- [ ] Space is the leader key.
- [ ] After pressing Space, if no follow-up key within 500ms, show which-key popup.
- [ ] Which-key popup shows all available leader key groups with descriptions.
- [ ] Leader key groups:
- [ ] `<leader>c` — Connect: quick connect, connect selected, connect all in group
- [ ] `<leader>f` — Find: fuzzy find connections, find by tag, find by group, find by host
- [ ] `<leader>s` — Sessions: list sessions, kill session, kill all, reattach
- [ ] `<leader>g` — Groups: list groups, filter by group, create group
- [ ] `<leader>i` — Import: import SSH config, import CSV, import JSON
- [ ] `<leader>e` — Export: export selection, export all, export group
- [ ] `<leader>t` — Tags: filter by tag, add tag, remove tag
- [ ] `<leader>v` — View: toggle tree view, toggle table view, toggle detail panel
- [ ] `<leader>h` — Health: check all, check selected, check group
- [ ] `<leader>p` — Password: show password, copy password, generate password
- [ ] `<leader>o` — Options: settings, themes, keybindings
- [ ] `<leader>?` — Help: keybindings reference, about
- [ ] Nested groups show sub-menus (e.g., `<leader>i` shows import options).
- [ ] F1.5 — k9s-Style Visual Layout**
- [ ] Top bar: Logo (NEXUS in cyan) + cluster/config info (right-aligned).
- [ ] Menu/hotkey bar: Context-sensitive key hints styled like k9s (<key>description).
- [ ] Title bar: Current view name + item count + filter status.
- [ ] Main content: Table or tree view filling available space.
- [ ] Status bar: Mode indicator (color-coded) + connection stats + flash messages + position.
- [ ] Command/filter input: Bottom line for `:` commands and `/` search.
- [ ] F1.6 — k9s-Style Table Rendering**
- [ ] Column headers with sort indicators (▲/▼).
- [ ] Age/uptime column with human-readable format (2d3h, 15m, 3s).
- [ ] Row striping for readability.
- [ ] Current row highlighted with cursor bar (like k9s).
- [ ] Wide mode toggle (Ctrl+W) showing additional columns (port, username, tags, identity file).
- [ ] Column width auto-sizing with minimum widths.
- [ ] F1.7 — Incremental Search & Filter**
- [ ] `/` activates forward search. `?` activates reverse search.
- [ ] Incremental filtering: results update as you type (like k9s).
- [ ] Search highlights matching text in the table.
- [ ] `n`/`N` cycle through matches.
- [ ] Search persists until cleared with `Esc` or new search.
- [ ] Filter bar shows active filter with clear button.
- [ ] F1.8 — Color Scheme System**
- [ ] Default theme: TokyoNight Storm (modern, cool blue-purple palette popular with neovim users).
- [ ] Mode colors: normal (blue), insert (green), visual (purple), command (yellow), replace (red).
- [ ] Protocol colors: ssh (green), rdp (blue), vnc (orange), telnet (yellow).
- [ ] Status colors: online (green), offline (red), degraded (yellow), unknown (grey).
- [ ] User-customizable themes via YAML skin file.
- [ ] Respect terminal colors option (use ANSI 16-color palette for terminal theme compatibility).
- [ ] F2.1 — SSH Jump Host / ProxyJump Chains**
- [ ] Per-connection ProxyJump configuration (single hop or multi-hop chain).
- [ ] ProxyCommand support for custom tunneling.
- [ ] Visual indicator in table showing connections that use jump hosts.
- [ ] Jump host health checking (check each hop independently).
- [ ] Dynamic port forwarding through jump hosts.
- [ ] F2.2 — SSH Port Forwarding**
- [ ] Local port forward (-L): map local port to remote host:port through SSH tunnel.
- [ ] Remote port forward (-R): map remote port to local host:port.
- [ ] Dynamic SOCKS proxy (-D): create a SOCKS5 proxy through SSH tunnel.
- [ ] Port forward configuration stored per-connection.
- [ ] Active port forwards shown in session detail.
- [ ] Port forward management view (list, add, remove active forwards).
- [ ] F2.3 — Session Recording & Playback**
- [ ] Record SSH sessions to asciicast v2 format (asciinema-compatible).
- [ ] Recording toggle per-connection (optional/required/disabled).
- [ ] Recording storage in configurable directory.
- [ ] Session playback via built-in player (rendered in TUI).
- [ ] Recording metadata: connection ID, timestamp, duration, user.
- [ ] Recording retention policy (auto-delete after N days).
- [ ] F2.4 — Connection Lifecycle Hooks**
- [ ] Pre-connect hooks: run shell command before connecting (e.g., VPN up, wake-on-LAN).
- [ ] Post-connect hooks: run shell command after successful connect (e.g., notify, log).
- [ ] Pre-disconnect hooks: run shell command before disconnecting (e.g., cleanup).
- [ ] Post-disconnect hooks: run shell command after disconnect (e.g., VPN down, log).
- [ ] Hook configuration per-connection or inherited from folder/group.
- [ ] Hook output captured in event log.
- [ ] Hook failure handling: abort connect, warn and continue, or ignore.
- [ ] F2.5 — Tmux Integration**
- [ ] Detect existing tmux session and offer to use it.
- [ ] Create named tmux sessions per connection group.
- [ ] Split pane support within tmux for multiple SSH sessions.
- [ ] Session persistence via tmux (survive TUI restart).
- [ ] tmux layout presets: single, hsplit, vsplit, quad, tiled.
- [ ] F2.6 — Quick Connect**
- [ ] `<leader>cc` or `:connect` opens quick connect prompt.
- [ ] Parse `user@host:port` or `ssh://user@host:port` format.
- [ ] Auto-detect protocol from port (22=ssh, 23=telnet, 3389=rdp, 5900=vnc).
- [ ] Option to save quick connection as permanent entry after connecting.
- [ ] Recent quick connects remembered (last 20).
- [ ] Template application to quick connections.
- [ ] F3.1 — Folder Tree View**
- [ ] Hierarchical folder structure for organizing connections.
- [ ] Tree view as alternative to flat table (toggle with `<leader>vt`).
- [ ] Folders are collapsible (za toggle, zM close all, zR open all — vim fold keys).
- [ ] Drag-and-drop reordering via move commands (`:mv connection folder`).
- [ ] Folder CRUD via commands (`:mkdir`, `:rmdir`) or leader keys.
- [ ] Nested folders up to 10 levels deep.
- [ ] F3.2 — Favorites & Recent**
- [ ] Mark connections as favorites with `<leader>ff` (toggle).
- [ ] Favorites view accessible via `<leader>fv` or `:favorites`.
- [ ] Favorites pinned to top of list (optional).
- [ ] Recent connections view (last 50) via `<leader>fr` or `:recent`.
- [ ] Most-used connections view (sorted by connection count) via `:frequent`.
- [ ] F3.3 — Bookmark/Marks System (vim marks)**
- [ ] `m{a-z}` set a local mark on current connection.
- [ ] `'{a-z}` jump to marked connection.
- [ ] `m{A-Z}` set global marks (persist across views).
- [ ] `:marks` show all marks.
- [ ] `` ` `` `` jump to previous position (before last jump).
- [ ] `Ctrl+o`/`Ctrl+i` jump list (back/forward navigation history).
- [ ] F3.4 — Navigation Bracket Keys**
- [ ] `]c` / `[c` — next/previous connection
- [ ] `]g` / `[g` — next/previous group
- [ ] `]e` / `[e` — next/previous error (offline connection)
- [ ] `]s` / `[s` — next/previous active session
- [ ] `]f` / `[f` — next/previous favorite
- [ ] F3.5 — Connection Templates**
- [ ] Define reusable templates with preset fields.
- [ ] Templates selectable when adding new connection.
- [ ] Template inheritance: connection inherits all template fields, user overrides specific ones.
- [ ] Custom templates via `:template create` or `<leader>ot`.
- [ ] F3.6 — Tags System Enhancement**
- [ ] Multi-tag per connection (already exists, enhance UX).
- [ ] Tag autocomplete in forms and commands.
- [ ] Tag-based filtering with boolean logic (`:tag web AND production`, `:tag web OR api`).
- [ ] Tag cloud view showing all tags with connection counts.
- [ ] Bulk tag operations in Visual mode (select connections, `:tag add production`).
- [ ] F4.1 — SQLite Backend**
- [ ] SQLite database as storage backend for large deployments (1000+ connections).
- [ ] Automatic migration from YAML to SQLite and back.
- [ ] Full-text search index for fast filtering.
- [ ] Transaction support for bulk operations.
- [ ] Database encryption (SQLCipher or application-level encryption).
- [ ] Config option to choose backend: yaml (default for <100 connections) or sqlite.
- [ ] F4.2 — Enhanced Import**
- [ ] Import from SSH config (already exists, enhance).
- [ ] Import from CSV with field mapping wizard.
- [ ] Import from JSON (RDM-compatible format).
- [ ] Import from PuTTY sessions (Windows registry or .reg file).
- [ ] Import from mRemoteNG XML.
- [ ] Import from SecureCRT INI files.
- [ ] Import preview showing what will be created/updated before committing.
- [ ] Merge strategy: skip duplicates, overwrite, rename.
- [ ] F4.3 — Export**
- [ ] Export to CSV, JSON, YAML.
- [ ] Export selection, group, or all connections.
- [ ] Export with or without credentials (credentials require master password confirmation).
- [ ] Export encrypted (master password protected).
- [ ] F4.4 — Credential Vault Enhancements**
- [ ] Multiple credential stores (personal vault, shared vault).
- [ ] Credential entries separate from connections (reusable across connections).
- [ ] Credential inheritance from folders.
- [ ] SSH key management: list, generate, import keys.
- [ ] SSH agent integration.
- [ ] Credential expiry warnings.
- [ ] F5.1 — Enhanced Health Dashboard (Pulse View)**
- [ ] Overview dashboard accessible via `:pulse` or `<leader>hp`.
- [ ] Connection summary: total, online, offline, degraded, unknown counts.
- [ ] Group health breakdown.
- [ ] Protocol distribution chart (text-based bar chart).
- [ ] Recent connection activity (last 10 connections with timestamps).
- [ ] Active sessions summary.
- [ ] Latency heatmap (connections sorted by response time).
- [ ] F5.2 — Connection Audit Log**
- [ ] Persistent log of all connection events (connect, disconnect, error, credential use).
- [ ] Log entries: timestamp, connection ID, event type, duration, exit code, user.
- [ ] Searchable log viewer with date range filter.
- [ ] Log retention policy (configurable days).
- [ ] Export log to CSV/JSON.
- [ ] Log stored in SQLite (separate from connections DB).
- [ ] F5.3 — Connection Notes & Documentation**
- [ ] Per-connection markdown notes.
- [ ] Notes viewable in detail view with markdown rendering.
- [ ] Quick note add via `<leader>n` or `:note`.
- [ ] Notes searchable via global search.
- [ ] Connection README: auto-displayed before connecting (optional).
- [ ] F5.4 — Custom Fields**
- [ ] User-defined key-value metadata per connection.
- [ ] Custom fields visible in detail view.
- [ ] Custom fields searchable.
- [ ] Custom field definitions configurable globally (field name, type: text/number/date/boolean/select).
- [ ] Custom fields displayable as table columns.
- [ ] F6.1 — Telescope-Style Fuzzy Finder**
- [ ] Activated via `<leader>ff` or `Ctrl+p`.
- [ ] Three-panel layout: prompt (top), results (left), preview (right).
- [ ] Fuzzy matching with scoring and ranking.
- [ ] Results update live as user types.
- [ ] Preview shows connection details of highlighted item.
- [ ] Multi-select with Tab (select and move to next).
- [ ] Action on selected: connect, edit, delete, copy, tag.
- [ ] Pickers: connections, sessions, tags, groups, recent, favorites, commands, help topics.
- [ ] F6.2 — Split Panes (Window Management)**
- [ ] `Ctrl+w s` horizontal split (table + detail).
- [ ] `Ctrl+w v` vertical split (two tables side by side).
- [ ] `Ctrl+w q` close current pane.
- [ ] `Ctrl+w o` maximize current pane (close all others).
- [ ] `Ctrl+w h/j/k/l` navigate between panes.
- [ ] `Ctrl+w =` equalize pane sizes.
- [ ] Split detail pane showing connection info alongside the list.
- [ ] F6.3 — Command Palette Enhancement**
- [ ] `:` activates command mode with autocomplete.
- [ ] Tab completion with cycling through matches.
- [ ] Command history (Up/Down arrows, persisted across sessions).
- [ ] Argument parsing with named parameters (`:connect --protocol ssh --host 10.0.0.1`).
- [ ] Command aliases (user-configurable, e.g., `:c` for `:connect`).
- [ ] F6.4 — Notification System**
- [ ] Flash messages for operations (already exists, enhance).
- [ ] Connection state change notifications (came online, went offline).
- [ ] Session timeout warnings.
- [ ] Credential expiry warnings.
- [ ] Notification history viewable in log.
- [ ] Desktop notification integration (optional, via notify-send).
- [ ] F6.5 — Undo/Redo**
- [ ] `u` undo last destructive operation (delete, edit, move).
- [ ] `Ctrl+r` redo.
- [ ] Undo stack depth: 50 operations.
- [ ] Undo applies to: connection CRUD, tag changes, group changes, config changes.
- [ ] Visual feedback on undo/redo (flash message showing what was undone).
- [ ] F6.6 — Bulk Operations**
- [ ] Visual mode select + operation.
- [ ] `:range` operations (`:1,10 delete`, `:tag add production 1,10`).
- [ ] Bulk connect (open multiple sessions).
- [ ] Bulk health check.
- [ ] Bulk tag/untag.
- [ ] Bulk move to folder.
- [ ] Bulk export selection.
- [ ] Progress indicator for bulk operations.

## Implementation Checklist

- [ ] Code follows project style guide
- [ ] Functions have clear documentation
- [ ] Error handling is comprehensive
- [ ] Input validation is performed
- [ ] Logging is appropriate
- [ ] Performance is acceptable
- [ ] Security considerations addressed

## Testing Checklist

- [ ] Unit tests written for all functions
- [ ] Integration tests cover main workflows
- [ ] Edge cases are tested
- [ ] Error conditions are tested
- [ ] Performance tests (if applicable)
- [ ] All tests pass
- [ ] Test coverage >80%

## Quality Assurance

- [ ] Code review completed
- [ ] Documentation updated
- [ ] CHANGELOG.md updated
- [ ] No compiler warnings
- [ ] Linter passes (clippy, etc.)
